        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In ∆AOX and ΔAOY, we already know that AX = AY, and AO is common to both triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.128,
            0.611,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we can show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle XAO = \\angle YAO"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then, by the SAS congruence condition, we can conclude that the triangles are congruent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.185,
            0.61,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To show this, we observe that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm{ABX} \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm{ABY}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This is so because AX = AY, BX = BY, and AB is common to both the triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.243,
            0.611,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{XAB} = \\angle \\mathrm{YAB},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle XAO = \\angle YAO"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because they are corresponding parts of congruent triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.628,
            0.138,
            0.918,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.628,
                0.138,
                0.918,
                0.309
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.299,
            0.595,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, AB is the perpendicular bisector of XY."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.33,
            0.52,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can have eyes of different shapes."
            }
          ]
        },
